WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.720
- I'm the first exoneree to be exonerated

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.220
by an Innocence Project, and
then go on to be a lawyer

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.900
for an Innocence Project.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.620
The best thing to do with your anger

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.790
is to use it as the fuel that drives you

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.706
to reach goals in life.

00:00:16.706 --> 00:00:19.610
My name is Jarrett Adams,
and this is my story.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.610
At the age of 17, I was
sentenced to 28 years

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.250
in a maximum security prison.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.008
I was falsely accused of a
sexual assault I didn't commit.

00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:35.170
And I realized very quickly early on,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.800
it had nothin' to do with
the truth, it was about race.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.290
If you can't afford to
prove your innocence,

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.090
the court affords an attorney to you.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.560
My lawyer convinced my family and I

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.290
that a no-defense theory was
the best theory of defense.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.930
It was a horrible idea, and
that defense contributed

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.445
to me bein' found guilty.

00:00:57.445 --> 00:01:00.260
(clock ticking)
(daunting music)

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.290
I was incarcerated in prison.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.760
So I was there for almost a decade.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.600
One day is too long when you're innocent.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.530
I was a kid.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:10.690
I was absolutely terrified.

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:13.450
My entire youth was gone.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.940
This is when boys become men.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.350
I missed out on all of that.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:28.540
I was, at a time, broken,
but when I continued to see

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.590
that my mother and my aunts weren't broken

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.730
and they were fightin' for my innocence,

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.510
I decided that if I didn't have the energy

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.590
to fight for myself, I most certainly

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.590
could find the energy to fight for them.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.270
I started to try to grasp the law.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.450
I would get law books, law journals,

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.830
and read about attorneys
who were litigating cases

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:49.950
in the State of Wisconsin.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.650
So I reached out to the Innocence Project,

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.380
the organization that
advocates and litigates

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.170
on behalf of the wrongfully convicted.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.080
Ultimately they accepted my case.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:02.660
The court unanimously decided
to overturn my conviction.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.750
I ended up enrolling
in a four-year college

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.090
where I studied criminal justice.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.070
After graduating, I obtained my law degree,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.470
and I became an attorney.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.910
I had the opportunity to
exonerate another person

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.066
and it was special to me,
because it was in the same state

00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:22.040
in which I was wrongfully convicted.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.284
I have now opened my own law practice.

00:02:25.284 --> 00:02:27.590
And I think that me comin' from a place

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.510
like the criminal justice
system, being wronged,

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.491
carryin' the stories and
gettin' to know other men

00:02:33.491 --> 00:02:36.990
who have been wronged,
what better advocate

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.690
could they have, but myself?

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.380
I strongly feel like this
happened to me for a reason.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.030
It was necessary to encourage
the greatness outta me.

00:02:51.877 --> 00:02:54.377
(bell chimes)

